WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.789 --> 00:00:17.132
Wendy now had a daughter named Jane, who loved to hear her mother's stories about Neverland.

2
00:00:18.233 --> 00:00:21.194
But most of all, Jane loved hearing about Peter.

3
00:00:22.475 --> 00:00:27.478
Wendy had bought her parents' house, so Jane slept in the same nursery her mother had slept in

4
00:00:27.578 --> 00:00:28.078
as a girl.

5
00:00:29.539 --> 00:00:33.890
But there were only two beds now—one for Jane and one for her nanny.

6
00:00:35.491 --> 00:00:39.573
Once a week, on the nanny's night off, Wendy would put Jane to bed.

7
00:00:40.534 --> 00:00:45.257
Then she would tell Jane wonderful stories about mermaids, fairies, and pirates.

8
00:00:45.277 --> 00:00:50.681
"Tell me about when you were a little girl," Jane would begin sweetly.

9
00:00:50.701 --> 00:00:55.604
"That was a long time ago," her mother would answer.

10
00:00:55.624 --> 00:01:00.728
"Tell me what it was like to fly," said the little girl one night.

11
00:01:01.696 --> 00:01:03.977
"You know, Jane, I can hardly remember.

12
00:01:04.418 --> 00:01:06.199
It was a long time ago."

13
00:01:06.219 --> 00:01:09.180
"Why can't you fly now, Mother?"

14
00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:14.924
"When people grow up, they forget how to fly," Wendy explained.

15
00:01:16.124 --> 00:01:20.187
She told Jane about the time Peter flew into the nursery looking for his shadow.

16
00:01:20.207 --> 00:01:26.450
"The foolish fellow tried to stick it on with soap and cried when it didn't work," she said.

17
00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:29.012
"But I sewed it back on for him."

18
00:01:31.804 --> 00:01:36.008
"Go on," said Jane impatiently, even though she knew all the stories by now.

19
00:01:36.028 --> 00:01:42.213
"And then he taught us how to fly and we flew to Neverland," said Wendy.

20
00:01:42.233 --> 00:01:45.436
"And what was the last thing he said to you?"

21
00:01:46.016 --> 00:01:46.637
asked Jane.

22
00:01:46.657 --> 00:01:53.022
"He told me he would return, and some night I would hear him crowing by the window.

23
00:01:54.083 --> 00:01:58.387
But then he forgot all about me," Wendy said with a sad smile.

24
00:01:58.407 --> 00:02:04.191
"Funny, I sometimes hear that crow when I am sleeping," said Jane.

25
00:02:05.672 --> 00:02:08.193
And then one night something unusual happened.

26
00:02:09.314 --> 00:02:11.676
It was a spring night, and Jane was asleep.

27
00:02:12.536 --> 00:02:15.879
Wendy was in the darkened nursery, sewing in front of the fireplace.

28
00:02:16.859 --> 00:02:19.141
Suddenly, she heard a crow.

29
00:02:19.941 --> 00:02:24.805
The window blew open and Peter Pan flew in, landing lightly on the floor.

30
00:02:24.825 --> 00:02:28.207
"Hello, Wendy," he said.

31
00:02:29.067 --> 00:02:32.117
In the dim light, Peter didn't notice that she had grown up.

32
00:02:33.258 --> 00:02:35.880
As usual, he was thinking mostly about himself.

33
00:02:36.921 --> 00:02:40.623
For a moment, Wendy wished she could be as small as she used to be.

34
00:02:40.643 --> 00:02:43.605
"Hello, Peter," she replied.

35
00:02:43.625 --> 00:02:46.647
"Is that John in the bed there?"

36
00:02:47.347 --> 00:02:50.269
he asked, pointing to the small body under the sheet.

37
00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:54.512
"No, John is not here now," she said.

38
00:02:55.553 --> 00:02:56.894
Peter looked more closely.

39
00:02:56.914 --> 00:02:58.535
"Is it a new one?

40
00:02:59.115 --> 00:02:59.956
Boy or girl?"

41
00:03:01.576 --> 00:03:04.678
"A girl," she replied, a bit fearfully.

42
00:03:05.478 --> 00:03:06.679
Peter looked at Wendy.

43
00:03:06.699 --> 00:03:08.700
"I've come to get you.

44
00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:10.161
Have you forgotten?

45
00:03:10.641 --> 00:03:12.182
It's time for spring cleaning!"

46
00:03:13.303 --> 00:03:16.204
She knew it was useless to ask where he had been over the years.

47
00:03:17.905 --> 00:03:21.147
Instead she said, "I can't come with you, Peter.

48
00:03:21.707 --> 00:03:23.308
I've forgotten how to fly."

49
00:03:23.328 --> 00:03:26.430
"I'll teach you again," he said.

50
00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:29.932
"Oh, Peter, don't waste the fairy dust on me.

51
00:03:30.984 --> 00:03:33.726
I'll turn on the light, and you'll see for yourself."

52
00:03:35.126 --> 00:03:37.808
When she turned on the light, Peter gasped.

53
00:03:37.828 --> 00:03:41.710
"You promised not to grow up!"

54
00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:43.011
he shouted at her.

55
00:03:43.031 --> 00:03:46.152
"I couldn't help it," she said.

56
00:03:46.172 --> 00:03:50.355
"I'm married now, and this is my little girl in the bed."

57
00:03:52.076 --> 00:03:54.337
Peter sat on the floor and began to weep.

58
00:03:55.398 --> 00:03:59.500
Wendy bent down to lift him up in her arms, but Peter backed away.

59
00:04:00.636 --> 00:04:03.619
Seeing him so hurt, she left the room sadly.

60
00:04:04.659 --> 00:04:06.161
Peter's sobs woke Jane.

61
00:04:06.781 --> 00:04:07.782
She sat up in bed.

62
00:04:07.802 --> 00:04:11.065
"Boy, why are you crying?"

63
00:04:11.505 --> 00:04:12.025
she asked.

64
00:04:13.627 --> 00:04:15.588
Peter rose and bowed politely.

65
00:04:15.608 --> 00:04:18.551
"Hello, I'm Peter Pan."

66
00:04:18.571 --> 00:04:21.893
"Yes, I know," said Jane.

67
00:04:21.913 --> 00:04:25.496
"I'm Jane, and I've been waiting for you."

68
00:04:26.677 --> 00:04:30.908
When Wendy returned, she found Peter sitting on Jane's bed, crowing.

69
00:04:32.049 --> 00:04:33.269
Jane was up in the air.

70
00:04:33.289 --> 00:04:37.631
"Jane wants to be my mother," Peter explained.

71
00:04:37.651 --> 00:04:43.173
"He does need a mother," Jane said, flying to his side.

72
00:04:44.654 --> 00:04:48.656
"Yes," Wendy said, "I know that very well."

73
00:04:48.676 --> 00:04:55.699
"He wants me to do his spring cleaning every year," Jane added, rising in the air with Peter.

74
00:04:55.719 --> 00:05:01.131
"Good-bye, Wendy," said Peter, as they headed out into the night.

75
00:05:02.113 --> 00:05:04.736
Wendy rushed to the window crying, "No!"

76
00:05:05.657 --> 00:05:12.686
She stood there, watching them fly away together to Neverland, growing smaller and smaller in the sky.

77
00:05:13.908 --> 00:05:16.992
"If only I could go with them," she sighed.
